acceptance_criteria: "Corpus includes a tiny scratch workspace, a real-shaped medium workspace, synthetic pm-mi2x scale fixtures, and continuity cases from pm-bwyw; each scenario records focus/query/claim state, expected item grades, token budget, and rationale; corpus format is documented and reviewable; phase-1 judgments baseline current structural context behavior before pm-4k6b changes ranking."
parent: pm-atfm
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Preserved historical judgments, added bounded medium-backlog scenarios plus measured representative 10k and scratch 100k cases with real claim history, respected scenario output budgets, and prevented baseline refresh from bypassing absolute thresholds."
expected_result: A reviewable corpus across workspace sizes and continuity cases proves relevant work remains visible within explicit selection and response budgets.
actual_result: "Seven standard and two large scenarios pass all accepted quality metrics at 1.0; large packets measure 1980 and 1961 tokens below 4000, independent selection checks pass, linked commands pass, and full coverage is exactly 100/100/100/100."
