comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-06T23:50:40.432Z",codex-agent,"Duplicate check: searched all statuses for context eval corpus/golden workspace/continuity judgments; only pm-atfm and closed search-eval work matched."
  "2026-07-09T19:10:24.967Z",codex-root-20260709,"Progress evidence: committed four-scenario corpus covers tiny scratch, real-shaped hierarchy, 100-item synthetic scale, and returning-agent continuity with explicit judgments, budgets, and rationales; accepted baseline is versioned."
  "2026-07-09T19:50:42.298Z",codex-root-20260709,"Verification: committed four-scenario corpus is stable through isolated SDK-backed trackers; tiny, real-shaped, synthetic scale, and returning-agent continuity scenarios all score 1.0 for NDCG, reciprocal rank, recall, continuity, and token adherence. Scale packet is 695 estimated tokens."
  "2026-07-09T23:53:30.023Z",codex-root-20260709,"Handoff after PR #487: the initial deterministic corpus and gate are merged and green. Item remains in_progress because its required representative 10k/100k corpus expansion and threshold calibration remain future work."
  "2026-07-31T00:18:13.858Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check and incident evidence: all-status search found this existing canonical corpus task plus parent pm-atfm and closed usage-feedback implementation pm-uwfs. PR #834 CI run 30592851802 failed the context gate on Linux and Windows after the fixed 2026-07-01 served/touched timestamps aged outside the usage-signal retention window; no new item was created."
  "2026-07-31T00:19:44.634Z","harness:codex","Fix evidence: the usage-feedback scenario now derives a single current touch instant and records serving exactly one minute earlier, preserving causal ordering while preventing retention expiry. Focused runner tests pass 5/5; the full required context-quality chain restores 1.0 nDCG/MRR/recall/continuity/token adherence and passes retrieval negative control, retrieval baseline, and all 91 token surfaces."
  "2026-09-17T19:41:41.354Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: preserved the five existing scenarios and added independent 300/800-token medium backlog probes, real SDK claim-history seeding, and reviewed 10k representative / 100k scratch shape scenarios. Initial large measurements passed every metric at 1.0. CI Gates (smokes) now executes the large corpus with a 10-minute step deadline. Baseline updates cannot write when absolute corpus thresholds fail."
  "2026-09-17T19:58:53.483Z","harness:codex","Full-suite verification passed 8974 tests in 704 files, with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. The corpus gate is covered by real isolated fixture execution plus negative controls for missing/dishonest budget receipts and a failing-threshold baseline-update refusal. Final large-corpus and required static runs are in progress before closeout."
  "2026-09-17T20:13:05.670Z","harness:codex","Large-corpus verification passed after real claim-history seeding: representative 10000-item fixture plus current anchor produced a 1980-token packet; scratch-shaped 100000-item fixture plus current anchor produced 1961 tokens. Both retained the required claimed anchor, stayed within the 4000-token packet ceiling, and scored 1.0 for nDCG, reciprocal rank, required recall, continuity coverage and token adherence. The independent 512-token executable-selection assertion also passed for each scenario."
  "2026-09-17T20:25:36.876Z","harness:codex","Both linked commands passed serially through pm test: quality:context-eval completed in 98 seconds, and the separately bounded 10k/100k corpus command completed in 192 seconds. The small corpus contains seven graded cases and the scale corpus two; every accepted quality metric remains 1.0. Final source coverage is running after these build producers completed."
  "2026-09-17T20:28:57.396Z","harness:codex","Final source coverage passed after the last implementation change: 8974 tests in 704 files with exact 100/100/100/100 and zero uncovered counts. Both linked context commands passed, all nine graded scenarios retain their accepted metrics, large tests are mandatory in CI, and baseline refresh refuses absolute-threshold failure. Hosted review and CI will validate the committed delivery head."
  "2026-09-17T20:33:23.938Z","harness:codex","Reviewed delivery: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1265 carries the completed corpus, required large-workspace CI step, SDK output-budget behavior, linked test evidence and structured closure. Implementation commit: 6a5e6826a. The PR retains exact-head hosted validation and review provenance."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-17T19:49:28.642Z","harness:codex",A baseline refresh must not bypass absolute quality thresholds. Pair graded ranking judgments with an independent byte measurement so a no-op token-budget flag cannot pass a generous packet ceiling; label large fixtures by measured shape as well as item count.
